{"pickle":{"id":"6e266bd4-6be1-4f18-8853-073d8c604519","uri":"features/ibr_encrypted_messages.feature","astNodeIds":["eea89630-ef92-4ac4-8c38-79bbd82f9bae","9c22a07c-ece9-4dfd-9d46-c6bb373b2179"],"name":"An encrypted message missing \"header.alg\" is rejected","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"36f9b9d8-460c-4895-a22c-d2aa6d3f7f91","text":"an encrypted \"enrollment-updates\" message","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["718b4ab1-e104-42f8-a132-cb2baddf4c5b","9c22a07c-ece9-4dfd-9d46-c6bb373b2179"]},{"id":"29fb4da6-eef4-4c73-aed3-a99fe6a90348","text":"its encrypted field \"header.alg\" is removed","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["7cf5664c-7739-43a7-b6e7-645efc3df659","9c22a07c-ece9-4dfd-9d46-c6bb373b2179"]},{"id":"cf58354f-7c99-497a-bd6d-3fd3bb9f6dbe","text":"the encrypted message should be rejected because of \"/message/header must have required property 'alg'\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["46aeeeac-d550-4533-ac59-284d14b9b0f9","9c22a07c-ece9-4dfd-9d46-c6bb373b2179"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"25fa0a3b-b66b-4309-a30e-8f95de0dee85"}]}}
{"source":{"data":"@method=POST @endpoint=ibr/sync/enrolled\nFeature: Check whether a beneficiary is enrolled in a programme (POST /registry/sync/enrolled)\n\nPRS.IBR.01: an SP-MIS queries the IBR to verify whether a person, a member or a household\nis enrolled in a specific programme before enrolling it in its own scheme. The IBR answers\nwith a minimal yes / no per beneficiary (EnrolledResponse.enrolled_status), never with the\nbeneficiary's records (data minimisation, PRS.IBR.01.2). Queries can be made at individual\n(member) level and at group / household level, for a batch of potential beneficiaries, and\nonce per programme.\n\nThe request carries an EnrolledRequest: enrolled_criteria with a query_type, a\nresponse_entity (Group or Member) and a query. The suite uses the spec's expression form:\n  { \"member_identifier\": { \"eq\": \"M100000001\" }, \"programme_identifier\": { \"eq\": \"DCI001\" } }\nwith \"in\" for batches, plus the idtype-value and predicate forms.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the \"enrolled\" endpoint\n\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: Successfully check that a member is enrolled in a programme\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"full\" Member in the \"child grant\" programme\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And every enrolment answer should have status \"succ\"\n    And the enrolment check should answer 1 item\n    And the enrolled status should be \"yes\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # PRS.IBR.01.1, 01.3, 01.4, 01.6: individual and household level, one programme at a time\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @functional @mock\n  Scenario Outline: The <type> \"<profile>\" is reported \"<expected>\" for the <programme> programme\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"<profile>\" <type> in the \"<programme>\" programme\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And every enrolment answer should have status \"succ\"\n    And the enrolment check should answer 1 item\n    And the enrolled status should be \"<expected>\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n    Examples: Individual level (member, PRS.IBR.01.3)\n      | type   | profile  | programme      | expected |\n      | Member | full     | child grant    | yes      |\n      | Member | widow    | pension        | yes      |\n      | Member | disabled | school feeding | yes      |\n      | Member | minimal  | child grant    | no       |\n      | Member | unknown  | child grant    | no       |\n\n    Examples: Individual level (person identifier)\n      | type      | profile  | programme   | expected |\n      | IBRPerson | full     | child grant | yes      |\n      | IBRPerson | newborn  | school feeding | yes   |\n      | IBRPerson | deceased | pension     | no       |\n      | IBRPerson | unknown  | pension     | no       |\n\n    Examples: Group / household level (PRS.IBR.01.4)\n      | type  | profile | programme   | expected |\n      | Group | full    | child grant | yes      |\n      | Group | large   | child grant | no       |\n      | Group | minimal | child grant | no       |\n      | Group | unknown | child grant | no       |\n\n    Examples: One request per programme (PRS.IBR.01.6)\n      | type   | profile | programme      | expected |\n      | Member | full    | pension        | no       |\n      | Member | widow   | child grant    | no       |\n      | Member | single  | public works   | no       |\n      | Member | full    | unknown        | no       |\n\n  @functional @mock\n  Scenario Outline: Enrolment in any programme: the <type> \"<profile>\" is reported \"<expected>\"\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"<profile>\" <type> in any programme\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And the enrolled status should be \"<expected>\"\n\n    Examples:\n      | type   | profile | expected |\n      | Member | full    | yes      |\n      | Member | widow   | yes      |\n      | Member | single  | no       |\n      | Group  | full    | yes      |\n      | Group  | large   | no       |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: The answer for the <type> \"<profile>\" is a coded yes / no\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"<profile>\" <type> in the \"child grant\" programme\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And the enrolled status should be \"yes\" or \"no\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n    Examples:\n      | type      | profile  |\n      | Member    | full     |\n      | Member    | deceased |\n      | IBRPerson | child    |\n      | Group     | single   |\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # PRS.IBR.01.5: a batch of potential beneficiaries in one request\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: A batch check of <count> <type> records answers every one of them\n    Given a batch enrolment check of the <type> records \"<records>\" in the \"child grant\" programme\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And every enrolment answer should have status \"succ\"\n    And the enrolment check should answer <count> items\n    And the enrolled status should be \"yes\" or \"no\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n    Examples:\n      | type      | records                         | count |\n      | Member    | full, widow, minimal, unknown   | 4     |\n      | IBRPerson | full, newborn, deceased         | 3     |\n      | Group     | full, large                     | 2     |\n\n  @functional @mock\n  Scenario Outline: A batch of <expected> beneficiaries is answered \"<expected>\" for each of them\n    Given a batch enrolment check of the <type> records \"<records>\" in the \"<programme>\" programme\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And the enrolment check should answer <count> items\n    And the enrolled status should be \"<expected>\"\n\n    Examples:\n      | type   | records                    | programme   | count | expected |\n      | Member | full, by person identifier | child grant | 2     | yes      |\n      | Member | minimal, unknown, single   | child grant | 3     | no       |\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Other query forms of the spec\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: An idtype-value enrolment check of the <type> \"<profile>\" is answered\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"<profile>\" <type> by identifier\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And every enrolment answer should have status \"succ\"\n    And the enrolled status should be \"yes\" or \"no\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n    Examples:\n      | type      | profile |\n      | Member    | full    |\n      | IBRPerson | full    |\n      | Group     | full    |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: A predicate enrolment check (process flow 2 form) is answered\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"example person\" IBRPerson written as a predicate\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And the enrolled status should be \"yes\" or \"no\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: The query of the EnrolledCriteria example is answered\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"full\" IBRPerson in the \"child grant\" programme written as in the spec example\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n    And the enrolled status should be \"yes\" or \"no\"\n    And the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: The <entity> response entity is accepted\n    Given an enrolment check of the \"full\" Member in the \"child grant\" programme\n    And the enrolment check asks for the \"<entity>\" response entity\n    Then the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message\n\n    Examples:\n      | entity      |\n      | Member      |\n      | Group       |\n      | Beneficiary |\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Requests that break the spec must be refused\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid enrolment check is rejected: <case>\n    Given a valid request\n    And the request field \"<field>\" becomes '<value>'\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n\n    Examples: Envelope and header\n      | case                 | field              | value        |\n      | missing header       | header             | <removed>    |\n      | missing message      | message            | <removed>    |\n      | wrong action         | header.action      | \"enrolled\"   |\n      | missing message_id   | header.message_id  | <removed>    |\n      | missing sender_id    | header.sender_id   | <removed>    |\n      | missing total_count  | header.total_count | <removed>    |\n      | invalid message_ts   | header.message_ts  | \"2026-10-13\" |\n\n    Examples: EnrolledRequest\n      | case                               | field                                     | value                                 |\n      | missing transaction_id             | message.transaction_id                    | <removed>                             |\n      | missing enrolled_criteria          | message.enrolled_criteria                 | <removed>                             |\n      | enrolled_criteria not an object    | message.enrolled_criteria                 | \"member M100000001\"                   |\n      | missing query_type                 | message.enrolled_criteria.query_type      | <removed>                             |\n      | unknown query_type                 | message.enrolled_criteria.query_type      | \"sql\"                                 |\n      | missing query                      | message.enrolled_criteria.query           | <removed>                             |\n      | empty query                        | message.enrolled_criteria.query           | {}                                    |\n      | query not an object                | message.enrolled_criteria.query           | \"M100000001\"                          |\n      | unknown response_entity            | message.enrolled_criteria.response_entity | \"Household\"                           |\n      | idtype-value query without value   | message.enrolled_criteria                 | {\"query_type\":\"idtype-value\",\"query\":{\"type\":\"UIN\"}} |\n      | predicate query without operator   | message.enrolled_criteria                 | {\"query_type\":\"predicate\",\"query\":{\"attribute_name\":\"member_identifier\",\"attribute_value\":\"M1\"}} |\n      | predicate query unknown operator   | message.enrolled_criteria                 | {\"query_type\":\"predicate\",\"query\":{\"attribute_name\":\"member_identifier\",\"operator\":\"like\",\"attribute_value\":\"M1\"}} |\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: A body that is not JSON is rejected\n    When the raw body \"enrolled?\" is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n","uri":"features/ibr_enrolled.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=POST","id":"7250f8af-d034-4ec8-8ada-c81251f69f09"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":14},"name":"@endpoint=ibr/sync/enrolled","id":"36abdb85-a4f2-4e74-8993-4961428c848d"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Check whether a beneficiary is enrolled in a programme (POST /registry/sync/enrolled)","description":"PRS.IBR.01: an SP-MIS queries the IBR to verify whether a person, a member or a household\nis enrolled in a specific programme before enrolling it in its own scheme. The IBR answers\nwith a minimal yes / no per beneficiary (EnrolledResponse.enrolled_status), never with the\nbeneficiary's records (data minimisation, PRS.IBR.01.2). Queries can be made at individual\n(member) level and at group / household level, for a batch of potential beneficiaries, and\nonce per programme.\n\nThe request carries an EnrolledRequest: enrolled_criteria with a query_type, a\nresponse_entity (Group or Member) and a query. The suite uses the spec's expression form:\n  { \"member_identifier\": { \"eq\": \"M100000001\" }, \"programme_identifier\": { \"eq\": \"DCI001\" } }\nwith \"in\" for batches, plus the idtype-value and predicate forms.","children":[{"background":{"id":"856ed5d1-1fae-4f3b-9442-82d2adb5c44a","location":{"line":16,"column":3},"keyword":"Background","name":"","description":"","steps":[{"id":"e883e531-31fd-47d8-9821-986aa28dc6da","location":{"line":17,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"enrolled\" endpoint"}]}},{"scenario":{"id":"63b70518-6b3e-44f4-b10f-23a4e8e4c92e","tags":[{"location":{"line":19,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"5deda906-4741-476b-b80c-5ad4dac02f7a"}],"location":{"line":20,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"Successfully check that a member is enrolled in a programme","description":"","steps":[{"id":"82442946-1f27-459a-a0b9-1fc8f3717640","location":{"line":21,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"an enrolment check of the \"full\" Member in the \"child grant\" programme"},{"id":"3abc211b-6a40-4208-af7e-fde957c6e1bf","location":{"line":22,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message"},{"id":"c26defc2-f6d9-4c7b-89f7-2e96b30bf951","location":{"line":23,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"9ae3db1a-9a9e-4896-b366-b96d485b11ed","location":{"line":24,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"d93a7ccd-79f9-4cb4-ae7d-ffc03e64553d","location":{"line":25,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have a JSON content type"},{"id":"92b28ce2-66b4-4a9f-9332-93d4329ec28a","location":{"line":26,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be received within 15000 ms"},{"id":"8c325bd6-59a7-4e10-938f-daaf7112bda5","location":{"line":27,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message"},{"id":"e376a95b-052b-4b30-afd3-40daf4cc5524","location":{"line":28,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"every enrolment answer should have status \"succ\""},{"id":"ad82f4b3-d9f6-4b59-9f44-078b65774711","location":{"line":29,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the enrolment check should answer 1 item"},{"id":"177db635-cff6-4134-89b6-dee26cbb770c","location":{"line":30,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the enrolled status should be \"yes\""},{"id":"e8fd7a21-fb20-43aa-b317-6b29ad229db5","location":{"line":31,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data"}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"cdee09de-486a-4530-bdb6-a45bce21ba7c","tags":[{"location":{"line":36,"column":3},"name":"@functional","id":"13b18c90-c12d-4685-8256-e5e3302e117c"},{"location":{"line":36,"column":15},"name":"@mock","id":"876916e9-79bf-431b-b6e6-619da7cda0f4"}],"location":{"line":37,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario Outline","name":"The <type> \"<profile>\" is reported \"<expected>\" for the <programme> programme","description":"","steps":[{"id":"b4902c3b-31ae-4a25-8061-5c9db99b5a1b","location":{"line":38,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"an enrolment check of the \"<profile>\" <type> in the \"<programme>\" programme"},{"id":"7af971c8-5757-4c3e-a9f9-835e6710e8b2","location":{"line":39,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"enrolled\" message"},{"id":"232e92cc-2f40-44a2-9b47-4874c610f0d9","location":{"line":40,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"edf59515-3321-4fa2-b963-b3a1f68ada54","location":{"line":41,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the response should be a valid \"enrolled-response\" message"},{"id":"7a459450-9191-42a4-9b4a-196f20462b37","location":{"line":42,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"every enrolment answer should have status \"succ\""},{"id":"24f38789-4e1d-4ab7-afad-a29e39b0a68e","location":{"line":43,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the enrolment check should answer 1 item"},{"id":"20c4180f-77d5-484a-aabe-91b893be21bd","location":{"line":44,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the enrolled status should be \"<expected>\""},{"id":"16e449da-e1a1-41f5-acba-efeac70a4be1","location":{"line":45,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the enrolment answer should disclose no beneficiary data"}],"examples":[{"id":"a9177927-65a4-4d18-83ac-59c61785bbdc","tags":[],"location":{"line":47,"column":5},"keyword":"Examples","name":"Individual level (member, PRS.IBR.01.3)","description":"","tableHeader":{"id":"dc232e6a-d5ed-4808-a5fb-394357bfe061","location":{"line":48,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":48,"column":9},"value":"type"},{"location":{"line":48,"column":18},"value":"profile"},{"location":{"line":48,"column":29},"value":"programme"},{"location":{"line":48,"column":46},"value":"expected"}]},"tableBody":[{"id":"d8f4da97-b347-4e2c-8570-80ec2912218f","location":{"line":49,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":49,"column":9},"value":"Member"},{"location":{"line":49,"column":18},"value":"full"},{"location":{"line":49,"column":29},"value":"child grant"},{"location":{"line":49,"column":46},"value":"yes"}]},{"id":"5c2d8ce7-9dea-4cb2-876b-3aad31c06a21","location":{"line":50,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":50,"column":9},"value":"Member"},{"location":{"line":50,"column":18},"value":"widow"},{"location":{"line":50,"column":29},"value":"pension"},{"location":{"line":50,"column":46},"value":"yes"}]},{"id":"b24e6ec0-b12b-4853-923e-c6104d6556e8","location":{"line":51,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":51,"column":9},"value":"Member"},{"location":{"line":51,"column":18},"value":"disabled"},{"location":{"line":51,"column":29},"value":"school feeding"},{"location":{"line":51,"column":46},"value":"yes"}]},{"id":"14ed7a6c-93dd-4d12-b025-cd317feffc4d","location":{"line":52,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":52,"column":9},"value":"Member"},{"location":{"line":52,"column":18},"value":"minimal"},{"location":{"line":52,"column":29},"value":"child grant"},{"location":{"line":52,"column":46},"value":"no"}]},{"id":"f9e7015b-a245-43d6-8f7e-5ccbac12be6b","location":{"line":53,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":53,"column":9},"value":"Member"},{"location":{"line":53,"column":18},"value":"unknown"},{"location":{"line":53,"column":29},"value":"child grant"},{"location":{"line":53,"column":46},"value":"no"}]}]},{"id":"61a59433-69fd-4b7c-a2b5-8872856f9b38","tags":[],"location":{"line":55,"column":5},"keyword":"Examples","name":"Individual lev