{"pickle":{"id":"410cf18d-626d-4d6a-9ad4-568226154593","uri":"features/ibr_member_data.feature","astNodeIds":["3a2275cf-945b-4a5f-bc9a-a52864e8e471","cd4ebc50-b26e-4908-9d92-f2eb05c02150"],"name":"Member attributes must be consistent: related to itself","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"af82ae9b-df25-4d41-9868-3c2624d85e56","text":"the \"full\" Member record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["7f428791-43c3-408b-b1cc-1fe8aa11b676","cd4ebc50-b26e-4908-9d92-f2eb05c02150"]},{"id":"105a405d-3458-4304-add1-3b30db663016","text":"its \"related_person\" attribute is set to '[{\"relationship_type\":\"SPS\",\"related_member\":{\"member_identifier\":[{\"identifier_type\":\"UIN\",\"identifier_value\":\"M100000001\"}]}}]'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["592ca5b0-79da-419b-8784-8cbffd112c50","cd4ebc50-b26e-4908-9d92-f2eb05c02150"]},{"id":"c7db4321-3aae-4bff-982b-6f7365343e87","text":"the record should be rejected because of \"relates the member to itself (UIN|M100000001)\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["bd2fc578-5b95-45ae-840c-a6d22c3914c2","cd4ebc50-b26e-4908-9d92-f2eb05c02150"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"02c1ce48-f1f7-4d22-8ee8-7a76f11b7d66"}]}}
{"pickle":{"id":"6663fcc6-361b-4fae-8b2b-f741850db1a5","uri":"features/ibr_member_data.feature","astNodeIds":["3a2275cf-945b-4a5f-bc9a-a52864e8e471","6ecd7a99-f74b-4f6a-a41d-ab57263a1131"],"name":"Member attributes must be consistent: related to itself by person id","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"409a0d89-85d7-477c-bb0f-1ead1d8f7a89","text":"the \"full\" Member record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["7f428791-43c3-408b-b1cc-1fe8aa11b676","6ecd7a99-f74b-4f6a-a41d-ab57263a1131"]},{"id":"2e6ae90d-a8b1-4873-807e-2d8a763004b8","text":"its \"related_person\" attribute is set to '[{\"relationship_type\":\"CHILD\",\"related_member\":{\"identifier\":[{\"identifier_type\":\"UIN\",\"identifier_value\":\"100000001\"}]}}]'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["592ca5b0-79da-419b-8784-8cbffd112c50","6ecd7a99-f74b-4f6a-a41d-ab57263a1131"]},{"id":"dc5f8f6b-1949-4d0a-b032-b523f2966351","text":"the record should be rejected because of \"relates the member to itself (UIN|100000001)\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["bd2fc578-5b95-45ae-840c-a6d22c3914c2","6ecd7a99-f74b-4f6a-a41d-ab57263a1131"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"02c1ce48-f1f7-4d22-8ee8-7a76f11b7d66"}]}}
{"pickle":{"id":"e3c9c854-5933-46ae-abb4-9f6a4a498438","uri":"features/ibr_member_data.feature","astNodeIds":["3a2275cf-945b-4a5f-bc9a-a52864e8e471","e15cd3e3-fe8b-47d7-9e76-acd69bafe81f"],"name":"Member attributes must be consistent: duplicate member identifiers","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"b2f21d60-8687-4be1-abee-35e08dd757d7","text":"the \"full\" Member record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["7f428791-43c3-408b-b1cc-1fe8aa11b676","e15cd3e3-fe8b-47d7-9e76-acd69bafe81f"]},{"id":"dfbd7140-d60e-4c9a-8269-32fe0b4b4908","text":"its \"member_identifier\" attribute is set to '[{\"identifier_type\":\"UIN\",\"identifier_value\":\"M1\"},{\"identifier_type\":\"UIN\",\"identifier_value\":\"M1\"}]'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["592ca5b0-79da-419b-8784-8cbffd112c50","e15cd3e3-fe8b-47d7-9e76-acd69bafe81f"]},{"id":"bbbdf8b8-0073-43b8-a6a7-0ecbba122f9c","text":"the record should be rejected because of \"member_identifier contains duplicates: UIN|M1\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["bd2fc578-5b95-45ae-840c-a6d22c3914c2","e15cd3e3-fe8b-47d7-9e76-acd69bafe81f"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"02c1ce48-f1f7-4d22-8ee8-7a76f11b7d66"}]}}
{"source":{"data":"@method=POST @endpoint=ibr/notify\nFeature: Receive enrolment notifications from the IBR (POST /registry/notify)\n\nThis API is exposed by the subscriber (SP-MIS, other registries). The IBR calls it when a\nsubscribed event occurs: a new enrolment (enrollement) or a change of enrolment status\n(enrollement_status_change: death, graduation, suspension), so that other schemes can\nreview eligibility (PRS.IBR.03.5). The suite plays the IBR: every notification is first\nchecked against the spec (including the IBR data rules of the beneficiaries, members,\ngroups and persons it carries), then the subscriber must acknowledge it.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the \"notify\" endpoint\n\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: Successfully receive a beneficiary status change\n    Given a notify request for a \"enrollement_status_change\" event carrying the \"suspended\" Beneficiary record\n    Then the request should be a valid \"notify\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: A \"<event>\" notification carrying the <profile> <type> record is acknowledged\n    Given a notify request for a \"<event>\" event carrying the \"<profile>\" <type> record\n    Then the request should be a valid \"notify\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n    Examples: New enrolments (enrollement)\n      | event       | type        | profile    |\n      | enrollement | Beneficiary | household  |\n      | enrollement | Beneficiary | individual |\n      | enrollement | Beneficiary | in-kind    |\n      | enrollement | Beneficiary | minimal    |\n      | enrollement | Member      | full       |\n      | enrollement | Group       | full       |\n      | enrollement | IBRPerson   | full       |\n\n    Examples: Enrolment status changes (enrollement_status_change: death, graduation, suspension)\n      | event                     | type        | profile   |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary | deceased  |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary | graduated |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary | suspended |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Member      | deceased  |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Group       | large     |\n      | enrollement_status_change | IBRPerson   | deceased  |\n\n    Examples: Event type spellings (process flows, namespaced spec example)\n      | event                                                    | type        | profile   |\n      | enrollment                                               | Beneficiary | household |\n      | enrollment_status_change                                 | Beneficiary | deceased  |\n      | spdci-common:RegistryEventType:enrollement               | Member      | single    |\n      | spdci-common:RegistryEventType:enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary | graduated |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: reg_records may be a single <type> object, as declared in the spec\n    Given a notify request for a \"enrollement_status_change\" event carrying the \"<profile>\" <type> record as a single object\n    Then the request should be a valid \"notify\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n    Examples:\n      | type        | profile   |\n      | Beneficiary | deceased  |\n      | Member      | full      |\n      | Group       | full      |\n      | IBRPerson   | deceased  |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: A batch notification covers every affected beneficiary (PRS.IBR.03.3, PRS.IBR.03.5)\n    Given a batch notify request for \"enrollement_status_change\" events carrying \"Beneficiary:deceased, Beneficiary:graduated, Beneficiary:suspended, Member:deceased\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"notify\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid notification is rejected: <case>\n    Given a valid request\n    And the request field \"<field>\" becomes '<value>'\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n\n    Examples: Envelope and event\n      | case                    | field                                       | value          |\n      | missing header          | header                                      | <removed>      |\n      | wrong action            | header.action                               | \"on-search\"    |\n      | missing header status   | header.status                               | <removed>      |\n      | missing transaction_id  | message.transaction_id                      | <removed>      |\n      | missing notify_event    | message.notify_event                        | <removed>      |\n      | empty notify_event      | message.notify_event                        | []             |\n      | missing reference_id    | message.notify_event.0.reference_id         | <removed>      |\n      | missing timestamp       | message.notify_event.0.timestamp            | <removed>      |\n      | missing data            | message.notify_event.0.data                 | <removed>      |\n      | missing reg_record_type | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_record_type | <removed>      |\n      | unknown reg_record_type | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_record_type | \"Programme\"    |\n      | missing reg_records     | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records     | <removed>      |\n      | an SR event             | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_event_type  | \"REGISTER\"     |\n      | unknown IBR event       | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_event_type  | \"graduation\"   |\n      | invalid locale          | message.notify_event.0.locale               | \"en-GB\"        |\n\n    @strict-data\n    Examples: IBR data in the notification\n      | case                            | field                                                                    | value          |\n      | enrolment status as a label     | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.enrolment_status               | \"Suspended\"    |\n      | assistance unit as a label      | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.assistance_unit                | \"family\"       |\n      | status change date not a list   | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.status_change_date             | \"2025-07-01\"   |\n      | programme without a name        | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.programme_identifier.0.programme_name | <removed> |\n      | benefit value with a currency   | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.benefits.0.benefit_value       | \"USD 50\"       |\n      | group type as a label           | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.group.group_type               | \"family\"       |\n      | member marital status label     | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.member.marital_status          | \"widowed\"      |\n      | person birth_date format        | message.notify_event.0.data.reg_records.0.member.demographic_info.birth_date | \"05-05-1950\" |\n      | member records with bad sex     | message.notify_event.0.data                                              | {\"reg_event_type\":\"enrollement\",\"reg_record_type\":\"Member\",\"reg_records\":[{\"demographic_info\":{\"sex\":\"Male\"}}]} |\n","uri":"features/ibr_notify.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=POST","id":"8df28692-adec-4b93-9175-9ff67bdcf127"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":14},"name":"@endpoint=ibr/notify","id":"7a9d15fd-84e1-4884-89bf-3080484e95f2"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Receive enrolment notifications from the IBR (POST /registry/notify)","description":"This API is exposed by the subscriber (SP-MIS, other registries). The IBR calls it when a\nsubscribed event occurs: a new enrolment (enrollement) or a change of enrolment status\n(enrollement_status_change: death, graduation, suspension), so that other schemes can\nreview eligibility (PRS.IBR.03.5). The suite plays the IBR: every notification is first\nchecked against the spec (including the IBR data rules of the beneficiaries, members,\ngroups and persons it carries), then the subscriber must acknowledge it.","children":[{"background":{"id":"1d7fe067-8833-49dd-a324-95d439f58b3a","location":{"line":11,"column":3},"keyword":"Background","name":"","description":"","steps":[{"id":"673b5865-291f-411a-b172-5ece8a0f3a4d","location":{"line":12,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"notify\" endpoint"}]}},{"scenario":{"id":"09830b0e-7b4c-4f05-be3d-66eda1e6f62a","tags":[{"location":{"line":14,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"afcee1b1-dd84-4320-b2d6-f804ea20d23d"}],"location":{"line":15,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"Successfully receive a beneficiary status change","description":"","steps":[{"id":"2026838f-d2d8-4797-b93b-ba6f5e2f954b","location":{"line":16,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a notify request for a \"enrollement_status_change\" event carrying the \"suspended\" Beneficiary record"},{"id":"72a1a891-88f8-447b-be1f-a85abaa8b597","location":{"line":17,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"notify\" message"},{"id":"d4481a5c-e7a7-4c4b-99cf