{"pickle":{"id":"36a222ad-3f0e-4743-83a0-4d5e5c62e0ec","uri":"features/ibr_programme_benefit_data.feature","astNodeIds":["7d5c79e5-3c30-4d80-9d0e-d5f64b319731","24d385bb-a2ef-4317-b10b-e3d3afd47b1b"],"name":"A recurrence must be consistent: until and count both given","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"d666f368-f81d-4764-949e-bd9c75358840","text":"the \"ten payments\" BenefitFrequency record","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["ad6a4c79-b9b2-4227-ad76-31bfb7a005c5","24d385bb-a2ef-4317-b10b-e3d3afd47b1b"]},{"id":"9b53f945-a223-49d9-9bdd-ba2b43392017","text":"its \"until\" attribute is set to '\"2025-10-31\"'","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["f1938b3f-d78c-4b8a-a69e-093e4b6b4c9d","24d385bb-a2ef-4317-b10b-e3d3afd47b1b"]},{"id":"2c1340fe-936e-4f47-b144-0e705a5e824e","text":"the record should be rejected because of \"gives both count and until\"","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["be43588b-6603-4bd6-8e75-5bb583221a6f","24d385bb-a2ef-4317-b10b-e3d3afd47b1b"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@data","astNodeId":"b16fdea8-e8de-4b01-ab5b-940ab91820c5"}]}}
{"source":{"data":"@method=POST @endpoint=ibr/search\nFeature: Asynchronous search of the Integrated Beneficiary Registry (POST /registry/search)\n\nThis API is exposed by the IBR and called by SP-MIS systems or other registries.\nThe IBR acknowledges the request, then delivers a SearchResponse to the on-search\ncallback given in header.sender_uri. The beneficiaries, persons, members and groups\ndelivered in the callback are checked against the IBR data rules.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the \"search\" endpoint\n\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: An async search is acknowledged\n    Given a search for the \"household\" Beneficiary by identifier\n    Then the request should be a valid \"search\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: Every kind of search is acknowledged: <search>\n    Given <request>\n    Then the request should be a valid \"search\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n    Examples:\n      | search                    | request                                                                                     |\n      | beneficiary by identifier | a search for the \"graduated\" Beneficiary by identifier                                      |\n      | person by identifier      | a search for the \"deceased\" IBRPerson by identifier                                         |\n      | member by identifier      | a search for the \"widow\" Member by identifier                                               |\n      | group by identifier       | a search for the \"large\" Group by identifier                                                |\n      | group of a person         | a search for the \"by person identifier\" Group by identifier                                 |\n      | beneficiary predicate     | a predicate search for Beneficiary records where \"the beneficiary is enrolled in the child grant\" |\n      | group predicate           | a predicate search for Group records where \"poverty_score is below 5\"                       |\n      | member predicate          | a predicate search for Member records where \"the member is a female widow\"                  |\n      | person predicate          | a predicate search for IBRPerson records where \"the person is a woman born since 1980\"      |\n      | beneficiary expression    | an expression search for \"Beneficiary enrolled in the child grant\"                          |\n      | member expression         | an expression search for \"Member who are female widows\"                                     |\n      | batch                     | a batch search mixing record types \"Beneficiary:household, Member:disabled, IBRPerson:unknown\" |\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Full async round trip: results are delivered to header.sender_uri\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @callback\n  Scenario Outline: The <profile> <type> is delivered to the on-search callback\n    Given a search for the \"<profile>\" <type> by identifier\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-search\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-search\" message\n    And every search result should have status \"succ\"\n    And every returned record should be a <type> record\n    And the result should contain the record identified by the query\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n    Examples: Beneficiaries\n      | type        | profile    |\n      | Beneficiary | household  |\n      | Beneficiary | individual |\n      | Beneficiary | suspended  |\n      | Beneficiary | deceased   |\n      | Beneficiary | in-kind    |\n\n    Examples: Persons\n      | type      | profile  |\n      | IBRPerson | full     |\n      | IBRPerson | minimal  |\n      | IBRPerson | deceased |\n\n    Examples: Members\n      | type   | profile  |\n      | Member | full     |\n      | Member | disabled |\n      | Member | widow    |\n\n    Examples: Groups\n      | type  | profile              |\n      | Group | full                 |\n      | Group | minimal              |\n      | Group | large                |\n      | Group | by member identifier |\n\n  @callback\n  Scenario: A paginated, sorted beneficiary search is delivered to the on-search callback\n    Given a predicate search for Beneficiary records where \"the beneficiary is enrolled in the child grant\"\n    And the search requests page 1 with page_size 2\n    And the search results are sorted by \"enrolment_date\" in \"asc\" order\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-search\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-search\" message\n    And every returned record should be a Beneficiary record\n    And every returned record should satisfy the predicate\n    And the search result pagination should report page 1 with at most 2 records per page\n    And the returned records should be sorted by \"enrolment_date\" in \"asc\" order\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n  @callback\n  Scenario: A mixed batch search is answered item by item in the on-search callback\n    Given a batch search mixing record types \"Beneficiary:graduated, Group:full, Member:widow, IBRPerson:newborn, Beneficiary:unknown\"\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-search\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-search\" message\n    And each batch item should be answered with its own result\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Requests that break the spec must be refused\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid async search is rejected: <case>\n    Given a valid request\n    And the request field \"<field>\" becomes '<value>'\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n\n    Examples:\n      | case                                     | field                                                    | value        |\n      | missing header                           | header                                                   | <removed>    |\n      | missing message                          | message                                                  | <removed>    |\n      | wrong action                             | header.action                                            | \"on-search\"  |\n      | missing sender_id                        | header.sender_id                                         | <removed>    |\n      | invalid message_ts                       | header.message_ts                                        | \"2026-13-01\" |\n      | sender_uri not a URI                     | header.sender_uri                                        | \"callback\"   |\n      | missing transaction_id                   | message.transaction_id                                   | <removed>    |\n      | empty search_request                     | message.search_request                                   | []           |\n      | missing search_criteria                  | message.search_request.0.search_criteria                 | <removed>    |\n      | unknown query_type                       | message.search_request.0.search_criteria.query_type      | \"sql\"        |\n      | unknown reg_record_type                  | message.search_request.0.search_criteria.reg_record_type | \"Programme\"  |\n      | invalid locale                           | message.search_request.0.locale                          | \"EN\"         |\n      | encrypted flag without encrypted payload | header.is_msg_encrypted                                  | true         |\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: A body that is not JSON is rejected\n    When the raw body \"{not json\" is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n","uri":"features/ibr_search.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=POST","id":"50679f28-cc51-4295-9ffe-5fccea194a58"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":14},"name":"@endpoint=ibr/search","id":"b979d9d0-8289-44e4-b2ca-635a2de2bcec"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Asynchronous search of the Integrated Beneficiary Registry (POST /registry/search)","description":"This API is exposed by the IBR and called by SP-MIS systems or other registries.\nThe IBR acknowledges the request, then delivers a SearchResponse to the on-search\ncallback given in header.sender_uri. The beneficiaries, persons, members and groups\ndelivered in the callback are checked against the IBR data rules.","children":[{"background":{"id":"3a4679bd-2a3a-4c40-9eff-8e72fb1d3703","location":{"line":9,"column":3},"keyword":"Background","name":"","description":"","steps":[{"id":"5080c47d-5e24-460c-a5c9-6def8da6f67c","location":{"line":10,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"search\" endpoint"}]}},{"scenario":{"id":"dc5027b0-a682-4c20-82c2-0e7f40c2c7af","tags":[{"location":{"line":12,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"22537253-735c-4191-ba25-5b92b659c635"}],"location":{"line":13,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"An async search is acknowledged","description":"","steps":[{"id":"39ae96c9-79fe-40f3-8913-df736081cc97","location":{"line":14,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a search for the \"household\" Beneficiary by identifier"},{"id":"6daf506a-725d-4198-be03-cff47494c4e3","location":{"line":15,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"search\" message"},{"id":"509a51e5-846b-4778-a5ae-dc4dc1fa4469","location":{"line":16,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"af75dcf7-8c1d-4051-9024-9e003e96f10b","location":{"line":17,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"1582dab3-edbf-48ff-bf94-f6e9e38edc63","location":{"line":18,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have a JSON content type"},{"id":"1c31d6cd-e936-48d4-a3dd-c94d7c5e35c7","location":{"line":19,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be received within 15000 ms"},{"id":"652af101-694f-472d-a207-56f1f6ee7b74","location":{"line":20,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\""}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"477f2ed1-b350-4298-8921-ce755c680f14","tags":[{"location":{"line":22,"column":3},"name":"@functional","id":"5ed089da-0276-4d07-b0a6-c37a0acbfa1a"}],"location":{"line":23,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario Outline","name":"Every kind of search is acknowledged: <search>","description":"","steps":[{"id":"5e47c698-2326-445b-b450-adec95fc1fd5","location":{"line":24,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"<request>"},{"id":"77b0dab3-caa9-43a7-937f-c6dc1f4ed0d7","location":{"line":25,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"search\" message"},{"id":"56fa96f3-f1e1-4fcf-8f43-43008c3c9796","location":{"line":26,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"ec60e3e7-4111-4426-a31f-68d0b155703f","location":{"line":27,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\""}],"examples":[{"id":"813f1251-a6ba-4c40-aed4-d3c657e251a6","tags":[],"location":{"line":29,"column":5},"keyword":"Examples","name":"","description":"","tableHeader":{"id":"6fe415ea-081c-47ef-905c-b92b812fe459","location":{"line":30,"column":7},"cells":[{"location":{"line":30,"column":9},"value":"search"},{"location":{"line":30,"column":37},"value":"request"}]},"tableBody":[{"id":"1edaf138-42d7-4558-