{"pickle":{"id":"49b37ced-a17f-4584-be67-9e9b11173009","uri":"features/ibr_search.feature","astNodeIds":["9eba4f50-c280-4d91-8ff9-6dd594fd389f","4af64206-5556-4fa4-8512-6d1cf2941306"],"name":"An invalid async search is rejected: encrypted flag without encrypted payload","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"7eea0fb3-94fc-4104-91f4-50d83e3475e3","text":"the \"search\" endpoint","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["5080c47d-5e24-460c-a5c9-6def8da6f67c"]},{"id":"a42c69a4-13a2-4b41-ac21-53617631e5ac","text":"a valid request","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["6359528e-58f6-4564-8683-ad13156e6313","4af64206-5556-4fa4-8512-6d1cf2941306"]},{"id":"30e5292c-69cf-4a32-9a47-9d571d8ad9d9","text":"the request field \"header.is_msg_encrypted\" becomes 'true'","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["5d180980-9dbb-4c70-82fe-2bdd6caa7576","4af64206-5556-4fa4-8512-6d1cf2941306"]},{"id":"49b8cbcb-b930-478d-8c88-b6c151588de9","text":"the request is sent","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["07f9c9c5-32de-47fd-819a-0dd7cb4d4463","4af64206-5556-4fa4-8512-6d1cf2941306"]},{"id":"3c568ba5-4006-4128-a5a9-f413b37da254","text":"the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["786fd506-a460-4104-b067-2c21f93e5aa5","4af64206-5556-4fa4-8512-6d1cf2941306"]}],"tags":[{"name":"@method=POST","astNodeId":"50679f28-cc51-4295-9ffe-5fccea194a58"},{"name":"@endpoint=ibr/search","astNodeId":"b979d9d0-8289-44e4-b2ca-635a2de2bcec"},{"name":"@negative","astNodeId":"9d5c66d4-0eab-4f34-961d-8168c3319438"}]}}
{"pickle":{"id":"891c22f6-d6ce-43bb-8ec4-ea3e3e3719f1","uri":"features/ibr_search.feature","astNodeIds":["0fc8e3ca-6b65-490b-a8f9-84dc9383c11b"],"tags":[{"name":"@method=POST","astNodeId":"50679f28-cc51-4295-9ffe-5fccea194a58"},{"name":"@endpoint=ibr/search","astNodeId":"b979d9d0-8289-44e4-b2ca-635a2de2bcec"},{"name":"@negative","astNodeId":"b85cee5c-b9ee-487e-90dd-9e4b151bd371"}],"name":"A body that is not JSON is rejected","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"f22bf49a-17f7-4724-87ef-01f543cd02c2","text":"the \"search\" endpoint","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["5080c47d-5e24-460c-a5c9-6def8da6f67c"]},{"id":"de13fd59-d3b6-4316-841e-642d8f33b1d0","text":"the raw body \"{not json\" is sent","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["3626a7b0-f7db-4702-88ab-dd0fbccdce22"]},{"id":"890c9374-a145-4a81-83e2-42ea5583b753","text":"the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["bb6b43d6-1126-4878-b4ee-fbd1c8d65723"]}]}}
{"source":{"data":"@method=POST @endpoint=ibr/subscribe\nFeature: Subscribe to Integrated Beneficiary Registry events (POST /registry/subscribe)\n\nThis API is exposed by the IBR and called by SP-MIS systems or other registries that want\nto be alerted when beneficiaries are enrolled or when their enrolment status changes\n(PRS.IBR.03.5: alert other SP-MIS when a change affects eligibility in other schemes).\nThe subscriber names the IBR event (RegistryEventType: enrollement,\nenrollement_status_change), the record type to be notified with and the beneficiaries to\nwatch (filter). The IBR acknowledges the request and delivers the subscription result\n(SubscribeResponse with subscription codes) to the on-subscribe callback.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the \"subscribe\" endpoint\n\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: A subscription to enrolment status changes is acknowledged\n    Given a subscribe request for \"enrollement_status_change\" events on Beneficiary records filtered by \"idtype-value\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: Subscription to \"<event>\" events on <type> records filtered by <filter type> is acknowledged\n    Given a subscribe request for \"<event>\" events on <type> records filtered by \"<filter type>\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n    Examples: Record types\n      | event                     | type        | filter type  |\n      | enrollement               | Beneficiary | idtype-value |\n      | enrollement               | Member      | idtype-value |\n      | enrollement               | Group       | idtype-value |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary | idtype-value |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Member      | idtype-value |\n      | enrollement_status_change | IBRPerson   | idtype-value |\n\n    Examples: Filter types (common QueryType)\n      | event                     | type        | filter type |\n      | enrollement               | Beneficiary | predicate   |\n      | enrollement               | Beneficiary | expression  |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary | graphql     |\n\n    Examples: Event type spellings (spec enum, process flows, namespaced spec example)\n      | event                                                  | type        | filter type  |\n      | enrollment                                             | Beneficiary | idtype-value |\n      | enrollment_status_change                               | Member      | idtype-value |\n      | spdci-common:RegistryEventType:enrollement             | Beneficiary | predicate    |\n      | spdci-common:RegistryEventType:enrollement_status_change | Group     | idtype-value |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: A batch subscription for several record types is acknowledged\n    Given a subscribe request for \"enrollement_status_change\" events on the record types \"Beneficiary, Member, Group, IBRPerson\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Full async round trip\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @callback\n  Scenario Outline: The subscription result for \"<event>\" on <type> records is delivered to the on-subscribe callback\n    Given a subscribe request for \"<event>\" events on <type> records filtered by \"idtype-value\"\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-subscribe\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-subscribe\" message\n    And every subscription should be confirmed with a subscription code\n    And every subscription should echo the requested event and record type\n\n    Examples:\n      | event                     | type        |\n      | enrollement               | Beneficiary |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Beneficiary |\n      | enrollement_status_change | Member      |\n      | enrollement               | Group       |\n\n  @callback\n  Scenario: Every item of a batch subscription is confirmed in the on-subscribe callback\n    Given a subscribe request for \"enrollement\" events on the record types \"Beneficiary, Member, Group\"\n    And the callback listener is used as sender_uri\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\"\n    And an \"on-subscribe\" callback should be received\n    And the callback should be a valid \"on-subscribe\" message\n    And every subscription should be confirmed with a subscription code\n    And every subscription should echo the requested event and record type\n\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  # Requests that break the spec must be refused\n  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid subscription is rejected: <case>\n    Given a valid request\n    And the request field \"<field>\" becomes '<value>'\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n\n    Examples:\n      | case                         | field                                                               | value         |\n      | missing header               | header                                                              | <removed>     |\n      | wrong action                 | header.action                                                       | \"search\"      |\n      | missing message              | message                                                             | <removed>     |\n      | missing transaction_id       | message.transaction_id                                              | <removed>     |\n      | empty subscribe_request      | message.subscribe_request                                           | []            |\n      | missing subscribe_criteria   | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria                      | <removed>     |\n      | missing reg_event_type       | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.reg_event_type       | <removed>     |\n      | an SR event                  | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.reg_event_type       | \"REGISTER\"    |\n      | Deregister is not in the enum | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.reg_event_type      | \"Deregister\"  |\n      | event in upper case          | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.reg_event_type       | \"ENROLLEMENT\" |\n      | missing filter               | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter               | <removed>     |\n      | filter not matching type     | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter               | [{\"expression1\":{\"attribute_name\":\"enrolment_status\",\"operator\":\"eq\",\"attribute_value\":\"1\"}}] |\n      | unknown filter_type          | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.filter_type          | \"sql\"         |\n      | missing notify_record_type   | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.notify_record_type   | <removed>     |\n      | unknown notify_record_type   | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.notify_record_type   | \"Programme\"   |\n      | frequency without end_time   | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.frequency.end_time   | <removed>     |\n      | frequency start not ISO 8601 | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.frequency.start_time | \"tomorrow\"    |\n      | frequency without cron       | message.subscribe_request.0.subscribe_criteria.frequency.frequency  | <removed>     |\n      | invalid locale               | message.subscribe_request.0.locale                                  | \"en\"          |\n      | missing reference_id         | message.subscribe_request.0.reference_id                            | <removed>     |\n","uri":"features/ibr_subscribe.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=POST","id":"8c7e0f1e-fab6-40cd-9379-62c7958a99b6"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":14},"name":"@endpoint=ibr/subscribe","id":"5b014a46-5585-4b1e-a418-00fd8dda73ba"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Subscribe to Integrated Beneficiary Registry events (POST /registry/subscribe)","description":"This API is exposed by the IBR and called by SP-MIS systems or other registries that want\nto be alerted when beneficiaries are enrolled or when their enrolment status changes\n(PRS.IBR.03.5: alert other SP-MIS when a change affects eligibility in other schemes).\nThe subscriber names the IBR event (RegistryEventType: enrollement,\nenrollement_status_change), the record type to be notified with and the beneficiaries to\nwatch (filter). The IBR acknowledges the request and delivers the subscription result\n(SubscribeResponse with subscription codes) to the on-subscribe callback.","children":[{"background":{"id":"8a3589f7-0b72-4512-8d3d-6cd54eb799b1","location":{"line":12,"column":3},"keyword":"Background","name":"","description":"","steps":[{"id":"4c6e9a6a-796d-40a7-8a26-b8943c322c22","location":{"line":13,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"subscribe\" endpoint"}]}},{"scenario":{"id":"4701f312-d99f-4577-9785-3e94cf090ba1","tags":[{"location":{"line":15,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"f24eacdd-c5ea-4a8c-9a08-99193d57f20f"}],"location":{"line":16,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"A subscription to enrolment status changes is acknowledged","description":"","steps":[{"id":"c3565bfd-cb59-488b-b645-2835a753b779","location":{"line":17,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a subscribe request for \"enrollement_status_change\" events on Beneficiary records filtered by \"idtype-value\""},{"id":"9aa98cf1-33c0-4b9b-b902-6b24bbfa4e05","location":{"line":18,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message"},{"id":"6fd35b4c-d418-4028-815c-5ec4dee7c5c9","location":{"line":19,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"0f41d502-9bc8-4247-bd34-bd0d0cca1928","location":{"line":20,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"43e04fff-a932-4ef8-9b32-0ce0a34c0b42","location":{"line":21,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have a JSON content type"},{"id":"ba23ce2a-3aff-426e-beac-4e10ec5725f8","location":{"line":22,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be received within 15000 ms"},{"id":"510ab746-6050-4baa-870b-33abfa055139","location":{"line":23,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid acknowledgement with ack_status \"ACK\""}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"a44bfc3d-9ac1-460c-af2d-ba6ee85184b1","tags":[{"location":{"line":25,"column":3},"name":"@functional","id":"6ae217a5-ea6a-44e0-a495-553515a889e6"}],"location":{"line":26,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario Outline","name":"Subscription to \"<event>\" events on <type> records filtered by <filter type> is acknowledged","description":"","steps":[{"id":"7444d91f-1814-4b8c-9f86-494b9e44f128","location":{"line":27,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a subscribe request for \"<event>\" events on <type> records filtered by \"<filter type>\""},{"id":"6f25f167-c5fb-4baa-b042-6a655ce5ef77","location":{"line":28,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"subscribe\" message"},{"id":"865461cd-050e-418b-b11e-7d0589df6fe6","location":{"line":29,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"b64e8988-0c3b-4936-9254-5a3156b2a750","location":{"line":30,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"O