{"pickle":{"id":"03295533-d729-4be3-8f37-0d7ce18b5947","uri":"features/ibr_sync_search.feature","astNodeIds":["bfcbeed4-4712-4422-af41-e9543016559f"],"tags":[{"name":"@method=POST","astNodeId":"93f9375f-f127-48e7-aa0b-534681638e64"},{"name":"@endpoint=ibr/sync/search","astNodeId":"28bd053e-b333-4f14-b3f0-325798b6bfa8"},{"name":"@negative","astNodeId":"aefb0967-b1ac-4f9a-9aba-c4e0f23b2e63"}],"name":"A body that is not JSON is rejected","language":"en","steps":[{"id":"d2e9fdb5-ea42-4323-83b1-66b6de89629f","text":"the \"sync search\" endpoint","type":"Context","astNodeIds":["142085d2-f228-4520-b9e1-235dbaba4f60"]},{"id":"0b2b5de0-e83c-415e-88df-3c1203e8fdc7","text":"the raw body \"this is not json\" is sent","type":"Action","astNodeIds":["040ab27e-4a5e-4769-afa9-17928b86bd7a"]},{"id":"042463a6-131c-4ea4-826f-78bfbdf1d806","text":"the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model","type":"Outcome","astNodeIds":["47a5f043-5784-43a0-81db-f5fce847da4d"]}]}}
{"source":{"data":"@method=POST @endpoint=ibr/sync/txn/status\nFeature: Synchronous transaction status check (POST /registry/sync/txn/status)\n\nThis API is exposed by the IBR and called by SP systems or other registries.\nThe response carries a callback header (action \"txn-on-status\") and a\nTxnStatusResponse whose txn_status matches the requested txn_type: a SearchResponse for\na search, a SubscribeResponse for a subscription, a ReceiptRequest (the published\nbeneficiaries) for a receipt.\n\n  Background:\n    Given the \"sync txn status\" endpoint\n\n  @smoke\n  Scenario: Successfully get the status of a search transaction\n    Given a transaction status request for \"search\" transactions by \"transaction_id\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"txn-status\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the HTTP status should be 200\n    And the response should have a JSON content type\n    And the response should be received within 15000 ms\n    And the response should be a valid \"sync-txn-status-response\" message\n    And the transaction status should be reported for a \"search\" transaction\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario Outline: Status of a <txn type> transaction looked up by <attribute type>\n    Given a transaction status request for \"<txn type>\" transactions by \"<attribute type>\"\n    Then the request should be a valid \"txn-status\" message\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"sync-txn-status-response\" message\n    And the transaction status should be reported for a \"<txn type>\" transaction\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n    Examples:\n      | txn type  | attribute type    |\n      | search    | transaction_id    |\n      | search    | reference_id_list |\n      | search    | correlation_id    |\n      | subscribe | transaction_id    |\n      | subscribe | correlation_id    |\n      | receipt   | transaction_id    |\n      | receipt   | reference_id_list |\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: The status of a search transaction carries valid beneficiary data\n    Given a transaction status request for \"search\" transactions by \"transaction_id\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"sync-txn-status-response\" message\n    And at least 1 record should be returned\n    And every returned record should be a Beneficiary record\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n  @functional\n  Scenario: The receipt of published beneficiaries carries valid beneficiary data (PRS.IBR.00.6)\n    Given a transaction status request for \"receipt\" transactions by \"transaction_id\"\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the response should be a valid \"sync-txn-status-response\" message\n    And at least 1 record should be returned\n    And every returned record should be a Beneficiary record\n    And every returned record should be valid IBR data\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario Outline: An invalid sync transaction status request is rejected: <case>\n    Given a valid request\n    And the request field \"<field>\" becomes '<value>'\n    When the request is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n\n    Examples:\n      | case                             | field                                     | value      |\n      | missing header                   | header                                    | <removed>  |\n      | wrong action                     | header.action                             | \"search\"   |\n      | missing message                  | message                                   | <removed>  |\n      | missing transaction_id           | message.transaction_id                    | <removed>  |\n      | unknown txn_type                 | message.txnstatus_request.txn_type        | \"disburse\" |\n      | unknown attribute_type           | message.txnstatus_request.attribute_type  | \"uin\"      |\n      | missing attribute_value          | message.txnstatus_request.attribute_value | <removed>  |\n      | reference_id_list given a string | message.txnstatus_request                 | {\"reference_id\":\"R1\",\"txn_type\":\"receipt\",\"attribute_type\":\"reference_id_list\",\"attribute_value\":\"R1\"} |\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: A body that is not JSON is rejected\n    When the raw body \"<xml/>\" is sent\n    Then the request should be rejected according to the DCI error model\n","uri":"features/ibr_sync_txn_status.feature","mediaType":"text/x.cucumber.gherkin+plain"}}
{"gherkinDocument":{"feature":{"tags":[{"location":{"line":1,"column":1},"name":"@method=POST","id":"a807a8de-e0d7-4d90-b4e2-22ac38f9af6b"},{"location":{"line":1,"column":14},"name":"@endpoint=ibr/sync/txn/status","id":"eeb616b8-7341-4e0f-90de-665cda3414a7"}],"location":{"line":2,"column":1},"language":"en","keyword":"Feature","name":"Synchronous transaction status check (POST /registry/sync/txn/status)","description":"This API is exposed by the IBR and called by SP systems or other registries.\nThe response carries a callback header (action \"txn-on-status\") and a\nTxnStatusResponse whose txn_status matches the requested txn_type: a SearchResponse for\na search, a SubscribeResponse for a subscription, a ReceiptRequest (the published\nbeneficiaries) for a receipt.","children":[{"background":{"id":"9ef58fc8-5b10-46c3-90db-caf0bf3cd885","location":{"line":10,"column":3},"keyword":"Background","name":"","description":"","steps":[{"id":"441e30b4-ef36-4fdc-bbad-3413767fcb37","location":{"line":11,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"the \"sync txn status\" endpoint"}]}},{"scenario":{"id":"d9eb0a81-5ba2-49b5-9f27-95576e3ec29a","tags":[{"location":{"line":13,"column":3},"name":"@smoke","id":"5bb73e93-94bf-4a58-802f-557d51e2a494"}],"location":{"line":14,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario","name":"Successfully get the status of a search transaction","description":"","steps":[{"id":"0ca4a822-5494-40f8-a869-42c6f20d1a6e","location":{"line":15,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a transaction status request for \"search\" transactions by \"transaction_id\""},{"id":"b0b9199c-83a8-49eb-9ad7-2224aa5e0d47","location":{"line":16,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"txn-status\" message"},{"id":"8d3a3965-a2e2-4c0c-a744-e74588ae60b9","location":{"line":17,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"be4c1ad0-d5f7-4713-a1b8-9d3cb3f2ee50","location":{"line":18,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the HTTP status should be 200"},{"id":"50973dd8-8c35-4415-b3b3-b9a73973d35c","location":{"line":19,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should have a JSON content type"},{"id":"9fa36c20-eeae-46b3-a529-387787f29552","location":{"line":20,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be received within 15000 ms"},{"id":"ea4e9b30-6d9f-43e1-9980-160e5db74983","location":{"line":21,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the response should be a valid \"sync-txn-status-response\" message"},{"id":"d1648537-923f-4a4e-8d08-44bc1c1b3dc2","location":{"line":22,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"the transaction status should be reported for a \"search\" transaction"},{"id":"a7b3b7b6-0b41-41d6-8278-edda8d892a77","location":{"line":23,"column":5},"keyword":"And ","keywordType":"Conjunction","text":"every returned record should be valid IBR data"}],"examples":[]}},{"scenario":{"id":"0ad579a0-2c2b-476d-a7f3-cfb90b0fd17e","tags":[{"location":{"line":25,"column":3},"name":"@functional","id":"e51b929a-360d-4cef-97f8-c221dbb8925a"}],"location":{"line":26,"column":3},"keyword":"Scenario Outline","name":"Status of a <txn type> transaction looked up by <attribute type>","description":"","steps":[{"id":"3d259efa-e4f2-4b08-956a-e934660d6983","location":{"line":27,"column":5},"keyword":"Given ","keywordType":"Context","text":"a transaction status request for \"<txn type>\" transactions by \"<attribute type>\""},{"id":"eeba690d-682c-4e4e-9538-73b128c43f52","location":{"line":28,"column":5},"keyword":"Then ","keywordType":"Outcome","text":"the request should be a valid \"txn-status\" message"},{"id":"ead37dd6-68fc-4db3-b4d5-f059ad86d1fc","location":{"line":29,"column":5},"keyword":"When ","keywordType":"Action","text":"the request is sent"},{"id":"006a49ad-3e62-40b7-9998-aec